  ('9c76079c-ce3e-4667-a1b6-120de05c74ab', 'kidney', 'caution', 'Oxalate: beets are high in oxalate, so heavy/chronic intake may raise kidney-stone risk in stone-formers.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 54a51570-df6b-47d1-91f1-d89fdd525dc2; signal "may raise", confidence high', 'draft'), -- beetroot
  ('8796577a-7d1e-4b24-845f-cae58049f104', 'breastfeeding', 'avoid', 'Contraindicated in pregnancy, breastfeeding, and infants.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e16639a0-014a-4e11-ba51-08d32f33d4ed; signal "contraindicated", confidence high', 'draft'), -- berberine
  ('8796577a-7d1e-4b24-845f-cae58049f104', 'children', 'avoid', 'Contraindicated in pregnancy, breastfeeding, and infants.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e16639a0-014a-4e11-ba51-08d32f33d4ed; signal "contraindicated", confidence high', 'draft'), -- berberine
  ('8796577a-7d1e-4b24-845f-cae58049f104', 'pregnancy', 'avoid', 'Contraindicated in pregnancy, breastfeeding, and infants. | NEONATES/PREGNANCY — berberine displaces bilirubin from albumin and can aggravate neonatal jaundice and kernicterus, especially with G6PD deficiency', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e16639a0-014a-4e11-ba51-08d32f33d4ed; signal "contraindicated", confidence high', 'draft'), -- berberine
  ('46f2bb5c-00dd-45a0-83a5-e6d55195904c', 'breastfeeding', 'avoid', 'Avoid in pregnancy and lactation (traditional vermifuges/naphthoquinones are prudently avoided', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 6c9bba37-65a3-4960-8288-65b9deb999a7; signal "avoid", confidence high', 'draft'), -- black-walnut
  ('46f2bb5c-00dd-45a0-83a5-e6d55195904c', 'children', 'avoid', 'Not for infants/children without clinical supervision.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 6c9bba37-65a3-4960-8288-65b9deb999a7; signal "not for infants", confidence high', 'draft'), -- black-walnut
  ('46f2bb5c-00dd-45a0-83a5-e6d55195904c', 'kidney', 'caution', 'Hulls are very high in tannins, which can cause GI upset, nausea, and (with heavy/prolonged use) theoretical hepatic and renal burden and reduced absorption of iron and other minerals.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 6c9bba37-65a3-4960-8288-65b9deb999a7; signal "theoretical", confidence medium', 'draft'), -- black-walnut
  ('46f2bb5c-00dd-45a0-83a5-e6d55195904c', 'pregnancy', 'avoid', 'Avoid in pregnancy and lactation (traditional vermifuges/naphthoquinones are prudently avoided', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 6c9bba37-65a3-4960-8288-65b9deb999a7; signal "avoid", confidence high', 'draft'), -- black-walnut
  ('d28979e9-214a-4c9c-ac75-9c944e2ea88c', 'breastfeeding', 'avoid', 'Animal studies show high-dose boron/boric acid is a reproductive and developmental toxicant (reduced fertility, testicular effects, fetal harm) — so megadosing is genuinely risky, and pregnant or breastfeeding women should avoid supplemental boron beyond dietary levels.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links c155070c-7ed2-48ac-93a0-b716973a0bd3; signal "avoid", confidence low', 'draft'), -- boron
  ('d28979e9-214a-4c9c-ac75-9c944e2ea88c', 'kidney', 'avoid', 'people with kidney disease can accumulate it and should avoid supplements. | No serious drug interactions are well documented, but data are limited — flag it to a prescriber if on hormone therapy or with renal impairment.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links c155070c-7ed2-48ac-93a0-b716973a0bd3; signal "avoid", confidence high', 'draft'), -- boron
  ('d28979e9-214a-4c9c-ac75-9c944e2ea88c', 'pregnancy', 'avoid', 'Animal studies show high-dose boron/boric acid is a reproductive and developmental toxicant (reduced fertility, testicular effects, fetal harm) — so megadosing is genuinely risky, and pregnant or breastfeeding women should avoid supplemental boron beyond dietary levels.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links c155070c-7ed2-48ac-93a0-b716973a0bd3; signal "avoid", confidence low', 'draft'), -- boron
