  ('d1cf9bfc-5f8a-4dc5-98c8-cdc9aca4b57a', 'anticoagulants', 'caution', 'changes the drug''s blood level (liver enzyme or transporter interaction)', 'Drug interactions: CBD inhibits CYP450 enzymes (notably CYP3A4, CYP2C19, CYP2C9), raising blood levels of many drugs — clobazam, valproate, warfarin and other blood thinners, some benzodiazepines, and others', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 0d7c1b50-31ae-4bb6-8837-d4470625996a; signal "none", confidence low', 'draft'), -- cbd
  ('d1cf9bfc-5f8a-4dc5-98c8-cdc9aca4b57a', 'antiepileptics', 'caution', 'additive liver strain', 'Liver: dose-dependent elevations in liver enzymes (ALT/AST) are documented, mainly at high pharmaceutical doses and especially when combined with valproate | Drug interactions: CBD inhibits CYP450 enzymes (notably CYP3A4, CYP2C19, CYP2C9), raising blood levels of many drugs — clobazam, valproate, wa', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 0d7c1b50-31ae-4bb6-8837-d4470625996a; signal "none", confidence low', 'draft'), -- cbd
  ('d1cf9bfc-5f8a-4dc5-98c8-cdc9aca4b57a', 'sedatives', 'caution', 'changes the drug''s blood level (liver enzyme or transporter interaction)', 'Avoid or use extra caution in pregnancy/breastfeeding, significant liver disease, and alongside other sedating agents or alcohol. | Drug interactions: CBD inhibits CYP450 enzymes (notably CYP3A4, CYP2C19, CYP2C9), raising blood levels of many drugs — clobazam, valproate, warfarin and other blood thi', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 0d7c1b50-31ae-4bb6-8837-d4470625996a; signal "caution", confidence medium', 'draft'), -- cbd
  ('96b661cc-808b-4996-a663-1eaba5949df9', 'anticoagulants', 'caution', 'additive bleeding risk', 'Anticoagulant interaction — chamomile contains coumarin constituents and there is a documented case and theoretical basis for potentiating warfarin/increasing bleeding risk | Chamomile contains coumarin constituents and may theoretically potentiate anticoagulants such as warfarin (monitor).', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 01258fff-e675-4ee8-9216-c6842b36bfb8, 3dfc18c8-e032-4638-b8b7-69578ca4eb10, 39338d30-7d0b-4e9e-8359-07282f2766f3; signal "theoretical", confidence medium', 'draft'), -- chamomile
  ('96b661cc-808b-4996-a663-1eaba5949df9', 'immunosuppressants', 'caution', 'changes the drug''s blood level (liver enzyme or transporter interaction)', 'CYP interactions — in-vitro inhibition of CYP1A2/CYP3A4 raises a theoretical flag for narrow-therapeutic-index drugs (e.g., cyclosporine), though clinical significance is unproven. | Drug interactions — may inhibit CYP450 enzymes in vitro and could theoretically raise levels of drugs like cyclospori', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 3dfc18c8-e032-4638-b8b7-69578ca4eb10, 39338d30-7d0b-4e9e-8359-07282f2766f3; signal "theoretical", confidence low', 'draft'), -- chamomile
  ('96b661cc-808b-4996-a663-1eaba5949df9', 'sedatives', 'caution', 'additive sedation', 'Drug interactions — because apigenin acts at the benzodiazepine/GABA-A site, additive sedation is plausible with benzodiazepines, ''Z-drugs,'' alcohol, and other CNS depressants. | CNS depressants — plausible additive sedation with benzodiazepines, alcohol, opioids, or other sedatives given the apigen', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 01258fff-e675-4ee8-9216-c6842b36bfb8, 3dfc18c8-e032-4638-b8b7-69578ca4eb10, 39338d30-7d0b-4e9e-8359-07282f2766f3; signal "additive", confidence high', 'draft'), -- chamomile
  ('fb664b30-dc70-44f9-9060-84ddc2a9421d', 'anticoagulants', 'avoid', 'additive bleeding risk', 'anyone on warfarin/anticoagulants should avoid it or coordinate with their prescriber. | High vitamin K content: Chlorella can antagonize warfarin and destabilize INR — a real, documented interaction', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e685bd2a-67ca-4fb0-a72e-07e7e35a81f4; signal "avoid", confidence high', 'draft'), -- chlorella
  ('fb664b30-dc70-44f9-9060-84ddc2a9421d', 'immunosuppressants', 'caution', 'immune effects may add to or oppose the drug', 'Avoid or use caution: pregnancy/lactation (the dioxin studies used it in pregnancy, but they are small/industry-run — not a green light without clinician sign-off), autoimmune disease (theoretical immune stimulation), iodine-sensitive thyroid conditions, and anyone on immunosuppressants or anticoagu', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e685bd2a-67ca-4fb0-a72e-07e7e35a81f4; signal "caution", confidence medium', 'draft'), -- chlorella
