  ('89d32ff6-480a-48a3-8c69-4661de5bdc79', 'anticoagulants', 'caution', 'additive bleeding risk', 'Because salicin is metabolized to salicylic acid (aspirin''s active form), the risk profile mirrors low-dose aspirin/NSAIDs: gastrointestinal upset/bleeding risk, and additive bleeding risk with anticoagulants/antiplatelets (warfarin, DOACs, clopidogrel, aspirin) and other NSAIDs.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 727ae5f4-f89d-4993-90d4-1c997509da41; signal "additive", confidence high', 'draft'), -- willow-bark
  ('89d32ff6-480a-48a3-8c69-4661de5bdc79', 'nsaids', 'caution', 'additive bleeding risk', 'Because salicin is metabolized to salicylic acid (aspirin''s active form), the risk profile mirrors low-dose aspirin/NSAIDs: gastrointestinal upset/bleeding risk, and additive bleeding risk with anticoagulants/antiplatelets (warfarin, DOACs, clopidogrel, aspirin) and other NSAIDs. | asthma with NSAID', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 727ae5f4-f89d-4993-90d4-1c997509da41; signal "additive", confidence high', 'draft'), -- willow-bark
  ('6c1cf520-9526-4fa9-a9a2-e5b7e4d2b065', 'antiepileptics', 'caution', null, 'INTERACTIONS: additive/antagonistic risk with anticonvulsants (may blunt seizure control)', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 310b3c0e-e679-472a-8015-7a85bf42ecb8; signal "additive", confidence high', 'draft'), -- wormwood
  ('8b8530b1-2ccc-44f2-916d-2eb2dca8b22d', 'antibiotics', 'caution', 'reduced or delayed absorption; separate the doses', 'Zeolite is a non-specific binder and ion-exchanger, so its main risk is that it does NOT bind only "toxins." It can adsorb and reduce absorption of MEDICATIONS and NUTRIENTS taken at the same time — separate from all oral drugs (thyroid meds, antibiotics, psychiatric/heart meds, etc.) by at least 2-', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e21b4ae1-ccfb-4c12-814a-4217fac888d8; signal "separate", confidence high', 'draft'), -- zeolite
  ('8b8530b1-2ccc-44f2-916d-2eb2dca8b22d', 'antihypertensives', 'caution', 'reduced or delayed absorption; separate the doses', 'Zeolite is a non-specific binder and ion-exchanger, so its main risk is that it does NOT bind only "toxins." It can adsorb and reduce absorption of MEDICATIONS and NUTRIENTS taken at the same time — separate from all oral drugs (thyroid meds, antibiotics, psychiatric/heart meds, etc.) by at least 2-', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e21b4ae1-ccfb-4c12-814a-4217fac888d8; signal "separate", confidence high', 'draft'), -- zeolite
  ('8b8530b1-2ccc-44f2-916d-2eb2dca8b22d', 'thyroid', 'caution', 'thyroid hormone effect', 'Zeolite is a non-specific binder and ion-exchanger, so its main risk is that it does NOT bind only "toxins." It can adsorb and reduce absorption of MEDICATIONS and NUTRIENTS taken at the same time — separate from all oral drugs (thyroid meds, antibiotics, psychiatric/heart meds, etc.) by at least 2-', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links e21b4ae1-ccfb-4c12-814a-4217fac888d8; signal "separate", confidence high', 'draft'), -- zeolite
  ('5f801965-5a3c-4c07-b05d-9deda7ed438c', 'antibiotics', 'caution', 'reduced or delayed absorption; separate the doses', 'Zinc reduces absorption of certain antibiotics (fluoroquinolones, tetracyclines) and can interact with penicillamine and thiazide diuretics (which increase zinc loss). | Zinc reduces absorption of certain antibiotics (fluoroquinolones, tetracyclines) and penicillamine — separate dosing by 2+ hours.', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 44944134-e9bf-4be2-a900-fb1d68925deb, cf7f312d-579d-4966-b3e1-fbd90640812a; signal "can interact", confidence high', 'draft'), -- zinc
  ('5f801965-5a3c-4c07-b05d-9deda7ed438c', 'antihypertensives', 'caution', 'reduced or delayed absorption; separate the doses', 'Zinc reduces absorption of certain antibiotics (fluoroquinolones, tetracyclines) and can interact with penicillamine and thiazide diuretics (which increase zinc loss).', 'rule-based extraction from atlas_links.safety_note by scripts/draft-safety-rows.mjs (no model); links 44944134-e9bf-4be2-a900-fb1d68925deb; signal "can interact", confidence high', 'draft'), -- zinc
